Marry Me is a 2022 American romantic comedy drama film
starring Jennifer Lopez, Owen Wilson, and Maluma.

12
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:47,538
Superstar Kat Valdez (Lopez) decides to marry Charlie Gilbert (Wilson), a math teacher holding a "Marry Me"
sign, after learning that her on-stage bridegroom, Bastian (Maluma), has been having an affair.

13
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
It is directed by Kat Coiro based on a screenplay by
John Rogers, Tami Sagher, and Harper Dill.

14
01:00:18,461 --> 01:00:24,461
Based on the 2012 webcomic of the same title by Bobby Crosby.

15
01:04:36,923 --> 01:04:42,923
The film was announced in April 2019, with Lopez and Wilson set to
star and Coiro joining the project as director.

16
01:08:55,384 --> 01:09:01,384
Universal Pictures acquired the film distribution rights in July 2019.

17
01:13:13,846 --> 01:13:19,846
Principal photography took place in Manhattan in October and November 2019.

18
01:17:32,307 --> 01:17:38,307
A soundtrack album of the same name by Lopez and Maluma was also produced.

19
01:21:50,769 --> 01:21:56,769
The lead single, titled "Pa' Ti", was released on September 24, 2020, and debuted at number nine on
Billboard's Hot Latin Songs, marking Lopez's highest chart debut in the United States since 2017.

20
01:26:09,230 --> 01:26:15,230
Marry Me premiered in Los Angeles on February 9, 2022, and was released in the United States
theatrically and simultaneously available on Peacock Premium on February 11.

21
01:30:27,692 --> 01:30:33,692
It was delayed twice from an original February 2021
release date due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

22
01:34:46,153 --> 01:34:52,153
The film received positive reviews from critics, grossing
$56.5 million against a budget of $23 million.

23
01:39:04,615 --> 01:39:10,615
On streaming, Marry Me became the most-streamed day-and-date title on Peacock.

